---
import Assignment from "../components/Assignment.astro";
import Glossary from "../components/Glossary.astro";
import PacketStepper from "../components/PacketStepper.astro";
import { tcpSteps, udpSteps, udpRecoverySteps } from "../components/packet-lessons";
import "../styles/course.css";

const tcpTransfer = [
  ["Connect", "The server waits on a port. The client connects, and TCP opens the connection with a handshake."],
  ["Send the label", "The client sends the file’s name, size, and SHA-256 fingerprint. The size tells the server how many file bytes to read."],
  ["Stream and save", "TCP delivers the bytes in order and retries lost data. The server keeps reading until it has the announced number of bytes, then saves the copy under a new name."],
  ["Check and reply", "The server calculates the saved copy’s fingerprint. It sends OK if the fingerprints match, or MISMATCH if they differ."],
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="description" content="Step through TCP and UDP animations, see how missing file data is recovered, and look up networking terms." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <title>Introduction to Computer Networks</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="wrap header-inner">
        <a class="wordmark" href="#top">Computer Networks</a>
        <nav aria-label="Course">
          <a href="#tcp">TCP transfer</a>
          <a href="#udp">UDP datagrams</a>
          <a href="#assignment">Assignment</a>
          <a href="#glossary">Glossary</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="top" class="wrap">
      <div class="intro">
        <h1>Introduction to <span>Computer Networks</span></h1>
        <p>Follow data between two computers. See what happens when it gets delayed or lost, and how a file transfer can recover.</p>
        <div class="intro-links">
          <a class="button primary" href="#tcp">Follow the TCP transfer</a>
          <a class="button" href="#udp">Try the UDP demo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section id="tcp" aria-labelledby="tcp-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="tcp-heading">Send a file over TCP</h2>
          <p>Think of a file with a label and a receipt. The client sends the label and file, then the server sends the receipt back.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="tcp-steps">
          {tcpTransfer.map(([title, detail], index) => (
            <li>
              <span class="number" aria-hidden="true">{index + 1}</span>
              <div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{detail}</p></div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <div class="note">
          <h3>Two confirmations</h3>
          <p>A TCP <a href="#ack">ACK</a> confirms that the receiving computer’s TCP stack got the bytes. The file transfer program’s <a href="#file-verdict">OK</a> confirms that the saved file passed the <a href="#sha-256">SHA-256</a> check.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lesson">
          <h3>Watch TCP open, recover, and close</h3>
          <p>Follow the <a href="#handshake">handshake</a>, then watch TCP fill a gap in its <a href="#byte-stream">byte stream</a>. See how both sides use <a href="#fin">FIN</a> to finish sending.</p>
          <PacketStepper label="TCP connection and recovery animation" steps={tcpSteps} sender="Client" receiver="Server" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="udp" aria-labelledby="udp-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="udp-heading">Send messages over UDP</h2>
          <p><a href="#udp-definition">UDP</a> sends each message as a <a href="#datagram">datagram</a>. See how <a href="#packet-loss">loss</a> and <a href="#reordering">reordering</a> affect what reaches the receiving program.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="demo-heading">Watch datagrams arrive</h3>
        <PacketStepper label="UDP loss and reordering animation" steps={udpSteps} />
        <div class="lesson" id="udp-recovery">
          <h3>Recover a missing UDP chunk</h3>
          <p>Illustration of the coursework’s <a href="#selective-repeat">Selective Repeat</a> design. The file transfer program confirms individual chunks and uses a <a href="#timeout">timeout</a> to retry a missing chunk.</p>
          <PacketStepper label="UDP application recovery animation" steps={udpRecoverySteps} />
        </div>
      </section>

      <Assignment />
      <Glossary />
    </main>

    <footer class="wrap">
      <a href="https://github.com/GadDev/binfo-networks-final-project">Coursework code and results</a>
      <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9293.html">TCP specification</a>
      <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc768.html">UDP specification</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
